_v(1)$</span>; equivalently <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p(tv)=c_v(t)$\">$\\exp _p(tv)=c_v(t)$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p(v)$\">$\\exp _p(v)$</span> is reached from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> by going ``distance&#x27;&#x27; <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|v|$\">$|v|$</span> in direction <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v/|v|$\">$v/|v|$</span>. Collecting the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> over <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp :O=\\bigcup _pO_p\\to M$\">$\\exp :O=\\bigcup _pO_p\\to M$</span>. By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23lem%3Apet-ch5-uniform-neighborhood\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-uniform-neighborhood\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368352d756e69666f726d2d6e65696768626f72686f6f64\">section 2</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23thm%3Apet-ch5-local-existence\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-local-existence\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368352d6c6f63616c2d6578697374656e6365\">section 2</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$O$\">$O$</span> is open in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$TM$\">$TM$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp $\">$\\exp $</span> is smooth; likewise each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$O_p\\subset T_pM$\">$O_p\\subset T_pM$</span> is open and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> is smooth. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-sphere-not-locally-minimizing","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-exp-diffeomorphism-properties","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-geodesic","title":"def:pet-ch5-geodesic","label":"def:pet-ch5-geodesic"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-exp-diffeomorphism-properties","title":"prop:pet-ch5-exp-diffeomorphism-properties","label":"prop:pet-ch5-exp-diffeomorphism-properties"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-exp-differential-nonsingular","title":"lem:pet-ch5-exp-differential-nonsingular","label":"lem:pet-ch5-exp-differential-nonsingular"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-normal-exponential-map","title":"def:pet-ch5-normal-exponential-map","label":"def:pet-ch5-normal-exponential-map"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-short-geodesics-segments","title":"thm:pet-ch5-short-geodesics-segments","label":"thm:pet-ch5-short-geodesics-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-radial-geodesic-segment","title":"lem:pet-ch5-radial-geodesic-segment","label":"lem:pet-ch5-radial-geodesic-segment"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties","title":"prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties","label":"prop:pet-ch5-local-isometry-properties"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_Geodes